course: dictionary
lesson: 6508
title: Needy: poor, or wanting a lot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Needy is an adjective with two main meanings. The first is about money and things: needy people are poor and do not have enough food, money or the things they need. «Defend the weak and the fatherless... rescue the weak and the needy» (Psalm 82:3-4) asks people to help those in this situation.
explain: The needy can also be used as a noun, with «the» in front. The needy means poor people as a group. Food banks and charities help the needy, and people give to needy families.
explain: Informal talk has a second meaning. A needy person wants a lot of attention, help or comfort. «My puppy is so needy — he follows me everywhere.» The puppy is not poor. It just wants lots of your company. Read the whole sentence to tell which meaning fits.
fact: Needy is an adjective: needy, needier, neediest.
fact: «The needy» is a noun phrase meaning poor people as a group.
fact: «Needy» can describe families who do not have enough money, food or things they need.
fact: Informally, «needy» can describe a person or pet who wants a lot of attention or comfort.
fact: In the Psalm, «the needy» means people in trouble who need help from others.
exercise: In «Food banks help the needy», what does the needy mean? | People who like to shop for bargains | *Poor people who do not have enough food or money | Teachers in the school canteen
exercise: Ella says her puppy is needy. What does she mean? | It has no money | It is very old | *It wants a lot of attention and company | It has lost its way in the park
exercise: Which word is the comparative form of needy? | neediest | *needier | needy
test: In «Rescue the weak and the needy», the needy most likely means: | Very clever people | *Poor people who need help | Rich kings who want gifts | Fast runners
test: Which meaning fits «My brother is so needy, he calls me every five minutes»? | Has no money at all | Lives far away from us | *Wants a lot of attention and help | Is very tall for his age
exam: Which sentence uses needy in the informal sense? | *«My cat is so needy that she sits on my keyboard all day.» | «Charities help the needy in every town.» | «Rescue the weak and the needy.» | «The needy family received a food parcel from the charity.»
